## Harness

- Golden set: fixtures/golden-orgs.json — 10 org profiles, 10 industries, 22–1200
  employees, 1–5 sites, standard mixes 9001×4 / 9001+14001×2 / 9001+45001×2 /
  all-three×2; eval-07 carries a justified ISO9001 8.3 exclusion (ORG-4 flow).
- Pipeline: the REAL deployed path per profile — saveOrgProfile → (exclusion) →
  generateImsManual → DocGenStateMachine → manual content JSON collected via
  getDocumentContent. Ten synthetic tenants tenant-eval-01..10.
- Grading protocol (model-evals blind protocol, adapted): 6 prose sections per
  manual, deterministic seeded selection + global shuffle (seed = sha256(HEAD)
  = 9ce994d...), sealed key committed-before-grading (round-3 key sha
  19721945162ee0256a07f096ca67af239f3f2669b20783a1267a5b054bbe5119).
  HONESTY NOTES: (a) grader = the architect AI (Claude), recorded in every
  score row; owner may re-grade from the committed sheet at the ACC pass.
  (b) single-candidate eval — there is no model identity to blind; the shuffle
  removes order/anchoring bias only; tenant identity is inherently visible in
  org-as-subject prose. Rubric dims (1–5): grounding, voice, clauseIntent,
  coherence, specificity. 1 = catastrophic (fabricated obligation/gibberish).
- Style validator: house-style-ci.test.ts — checker.ts rules run over EVERY
  prose section of the committed live manuals (no shall / bullets /
  placeholders / second person / banned fragments / inline fact markers /
  org-as-subject / citation presence) + negative pins for every rule so a
  checker regression also fails CI + gap-sections-carry-no-prose pin.
  Scope note: factRef RESOLUTION stays a runtime/ledger check (BC-4).

## Three rounds — what the harness caught (the point of the exercise)

### Round 1 (system as of 9ce994d): mean 4.420, zero 1s — PASS, with findings
- 10 runs COMPLETE, 107 prose sections, 24s median.
- F1 REAL FACT-PIPELINE BUG: facts.ts `present(false) === true` → orgs with
  manualExists:false were fed the fact "maintains an existing quality manual";
  the model faithfully CITED the lie (BC-4 passed — the fact was provided).
  4 fabrications across the corpus. Root: missing boolean ternary (the
  designResponsibility field right above had it).
- F2 SYSTEMIC STYLE LEAK: inline fact markers "(F1, F3)" echoed into prose —
  10/107 sections, 35 instances — would print in customer PDFs. checker.ts had
  no rule for it.
- F3 minor: future-tense section (V&V 4.4), tri-standard repetition in shared
  sections, puffery adverbs. Backlog, not blocking.

### Fixes (deployed to AiStack between rounds)
1. facts.ts: manualExists ternary (false → "does not yet have a quality
   manual; this document establishes it"). Pinned by 3 unit tests.
2. checker.ts: INLINE_FACT_MARKER rule — deterministic, feeds the compose
   retry loop (runtime self-correction) AND the CI validator. Negative pin.
3. compose prompt: citations in factRefs only, never in text.

### Round 2 (interim): fabrications 4→0, markers 10→0 — and a NEW class caught
- F4 RUN-FATALITY BUG: eval-09's 8.3 section — the model over-corrected on the
  new prompt and returned EMPTY factRefs; ai-invoker schema validation failed
  terminally; the error escaped ComposeSection's failure handling, KILLED the
  whole execution (ExecutionFailed) and left the run stuck 'running'.
  Meanwhile eval-08's 7.5 checker-exhaustion failure was handled correctly
  (section failed, run PARTIAL) — a resilience ASYMMETRY.
- Fixes: compose-section wraps the invoker call — terminal invoker error now
  routes into the SAME honest path as checker exhaustion (section 'failed',
  run finishes PARTIAL, never silently gapped, never run-fatal). Regression
  test reproduces the exact eval-09 payload. Prompt v3 makes BOTH factRefs
  requirements explicit. Stuck run 5d6f1cea marked 'failed' by architect
  (rds-data, 1 row).

### Round 3 (OFFICIAL — final deployed code, all 10 regenerated)
- 9 COMPLETE + 1 PARTIAL (eval-05: 2 sections failed HONESTLY under retry
  exhaustion — the new resilience path exercised live). No aborts, no stuck
  runs. 115 prose sections. inline markers 0. manual-exists fabrications 0.
- Grading: mean 4.530/5, zero 1s, three 2s → NFR-3 PASS.
- F5 (the three 2s, named follow-up — owner-visible): orgs with
  designResponsibility:false and NO recorded 8.3 exclusion sometimes get
  fabricated design-process prose for 8.3 (FreshCrate/Meridian/SteelSpan this
  round; model variance — the same orgs produced honest "does not design"
  prose in round 1). eval-07 (recorded ORG-4 exclusion) gets clean
  NA-JUSTIFIED by construction — the DESIGNED path works. Recommended fix is
  product-level: wizard nudge to record the 8.3 exclusion when
  designResponsibility=false (auto-NA would bypass ORG-4's
  exclude-with-justification governance — owner decision, not an in-lane
  patch). Optional prompt hardening as a cheaper mitigation.

